{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "AI Code Review & QA Agent",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/acme/ai-code-review",
          "version": "deepseek-v4-flash",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "acr/bug",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "saveOrder reports success without awaiting the insert, so a failed write is silently reported as ok"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "bug",
                  "agent"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "acr/testing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "New module's orderQuery and saveOrder have no test coverage"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "testing",
                  "agent"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/bug",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "saveOrder reports success without awaiting the insert, so a failed write is silently reported as ok\n\n`saveOrder` is declared `async` but never awaits `store.insert(...)`. If the store's insert is asynchronous (returns a promise, as most DB/ORM clients do), a rejected write becomes an unhandled rejection while the caller still receives `{ ok: true }` — the checkout flow would treat a lost order as persisted. Fix: `await store.insert({ id: randomUUID(), ...order });` and let the rejection propagate (or catch it and return `{ ok: false }`)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/pricing.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 14
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "medium",
            "confidence": 0.6,
            "status": "validated",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "583a82cd-78f3-4fe0-ac0b-e4377ae16c05"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/testing",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "New module's orderQuery and saveOrder have no test coverage\n\nThe test file imports only `applyDiscount` and `isPaid`, so two of the four helpers added by this PR (`orderQuery`, `saveOrder`) are never exercised. `orderQuery` in particular builds a query by string concatenation and `saveOrder` is the only write path; both are exactly the functions where a regression would be silent. Add at least one test per helper (e.g. assert the generated query for a tenant id, and assert the object passed to a fake store)."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "test/pricing.test.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 4
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "low",
            "confidence": 0.9,
            "status": "validated",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "583a82cd-78f3-4fe0-ac0b-e4377ae16c05"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "acr/bug",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "applyDiscount accepts out-of-range discountPercent with no guard\n\n`applyDiscount` performs no validation of `discountPercent`, so a value outside [0, 1] silently produces a nonsensical total (e.g. `applyDiscount(100, 1.5)` returns -50, and a negative percent increases the total). Since the parameter is named `discountPercent` but used as a fraction, callers passing `10` for 10% get -900 — the behaviour the new test pins. Add a range check (throw or clamp) and rename the parameter to `discountRate`/`discountFraction` so the unit is unambiguous."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/pricing.js"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 6
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "severity": "info",
            "confidence": 0.6,
            "status": "validated",
            "source": "agent",
            "reviewRunId": "583a82cd-78f3-4fe0-ac0b-e4377ae16c05"
          }
        }
      ],
      "originalUriBaseIds": {
        "REPO_ROOT": {
          "uri": "https://github.com/KamerrEzz/argus-sample/tree/0d0f97cf177e6f57a631ad5677a70320ccbfefd0/"
        }
      },
      "columnKind": "utf16CodeUnits"
    }
  ]
}